IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-gunpowder`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-gunpowder.l4 (sections 64 and
-- 65).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before the assertion
-- was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: gunpowder`

§§ `Section 64`

-- knowingly had or made a thing of the listed kinds, intended by means of it to commit an
-- offence, made it to enable another person to commit one, how the text classifies that offence
`s64 own intent, a felony` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, felony
`s64 to enable another, a felony` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, felony
`s64 intent to commit a misdemeanor` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, misdemeanor
`s64 intent to commit an offence the text does not classify` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `no classification stated`
`s64 intent to commit an offence the text calls only an offence` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `an offence, with no further classification`
`s64 not knowingly` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, felony
`s64 no intent either way` MEANS `Conduct under section 64` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, felony

#ASSERT `s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 own intent, a felony`
#ASSERT `s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 to enable another, a felony`
-- the felony must be one "in this Act mentioned": a misdemeanor, or an offence the text
-- does not call a felony, is outside the section
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 intent to commit a misdemeanor`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 intent to commit an offence the text does not classify`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 intent to commit an offence the text calls only an offence`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 not knowingly`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` `s64 no intent either way`)
#ASSERT `s 64: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
-- two years = 24 months
#ASSERT `s 64: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 65`

-- a thing is suspected to be made, kept or carried for a felony of the Act, cause assigned
-- upon oath, the justice accepts the cause as reasonable, the place is one listed, the
-- thing was found upon the search, the executing person has good cause to suspect it
`s65 warrant and seizure` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s65 warrant, nothing found` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s65 found but no good cause to suspect` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s65 nothing suspected` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s65 no cause assigned upon oath` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s65 the justice does not accept the cause` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s65 not a listed place` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s65 found and good cause, but no warrant could issue` MEANS `Search under section 65` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 warrant and seizure`
#ASSERT `s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 warrant, nothing found`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 nothing suspected`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 no cause assigned upon oath`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 the justice does not accept the cause`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant to search the place` `s65 not a listed place`)
#ASSERT `s 65: the thing and its receptacles may be seized, removed and detained` `s65 warrant and seizure`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: the thing and its receptacles may be seized, removed and detained` `s65 warrant, nothing found`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: the thing and its receptacles may be seized, removed and detained` `s65 found but no good cause to suspect`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65: the thing and its receptacles may be seized, removed and detained` `s65 found and good cause, but no warrant could issue`)
